  {
   "verse_number": 2,
   "source_text_master": [
    "(emana dayāla to nāi he, māra khe’ye prema deya)",
    "(ore) aparādha dūre yā’be, pā’be premadhana",
    "(o nāme aparādha[FLAG_HYPHEN_ALPHA]bicāra to nāi he)",
    "(takhana) kṛṣṇanāme ruci ha’be, ghucibe bandhana 2"
   ],
   "translations": [
    {
     "language_code": "eng",
     "text": [
      "(There is no one as merciful as Nitāi, for despite being beaten, He bestowed prema.) By chanting Their names, your offenses will go far away and you will obtain the treasure of prema. (There is no consideration of offenses in chanting Their holy names.) (Then) you will develop a taste for kṛṣṇa-nāma, and your bondage [to material existence] will be destroyed."
     ]
    }
   ],
